  "notes": "Rebuilt both venvs with Python 3.11 because piper-phonemize has no Linux wheel for 3.12. Compiled the monotonic_align Cython extension into each venv (kt_ext/ plus a .pth that registers it in sys.modules), without touching src. The workload trains a tiny VitsModel for 3 steps on synthetic data with Trainer.fit. Head uses manual optimization. On base, PL 2.5 rejects the optimizer_idx-style training_step with a RuntimeError, so the workload falls back to calling training_step(batch, i, idx) with the model's own optimizers. The digests differ as expected. Coverage of changed lines: head 92%, base 86%."
